#!/usr/bin/env ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

=begin
2links - URL Extractor, Canonicalizer, and Deduplicator
========================================================

## SPECIFICATION

2links is a universal command-line tool that extracts, normalizes, and deduplicates URLs
from any UTF8 text, regardless of format (HTML, Markdown, code, YAML, JSON, etc.).
It canonicalizes URLs to a standard form and removes duplicates that point to the same
resource, preferring HTTPS over HTTP and sorting output alphabetically.

## SUPPORTED SCHEMES

- http:// and https://
- ftp://

## CONTRACT

### Input
- Any UTF8 text containing URLs (HTML, Markdown, code, YAML, JSON, etc.)
- Accepts from stdin or file argument
- Max URL length: 2048 characters (standard)
- Format-agnostic: works with mixed content

### Processing Pipeline
1. **Extraction:** Regex scan for scheme://host:port/path pattern (format-agnostic)
2. **Validation:** URI.parse() with strict scheme whitelist
3. **Canonicalization:** Normalize scheme/host/path, strip trailing slashes
4. **Deduplication:** Group by scheme-agnostic key, prefer https
5. **Sorting:** Alphabetical by canonical URL
6. **Output:** Text (default) or JSON format

### Canonicalization Rules

1. Parse URL with URI.parse()
2. Validate scheme (http|https|ftp only)
3. Lowercase scheme and hostname
4. Strip trailing slash (except for root "/")
5. Query params/fragments: PRESERVED in original, OMITTED in canonical key
6. User info (user:pass@): STRIPPED and WARNED
7. Default ports omitted (80→http, 443→https, 21→ftp)

### Deduplication Logic

- **Key:** Scheme-agnostic (host:port/path)
- **Preference:** HTTPS > HTTP > FTP
- **Fallback:** Count most common representation

Example:
  Input:  https://github.com/user/repo
          http://github.com/user/repo
          https://github.com/user/repo/
  Output: https://github.com/user/repo (single canonical, https preferred)

### Output Formats

#### Text (default)
One canonical URL per line, sorted alphabetically.
Clean, Unix-friendly, easily piped.

#### JSON (--format json)
Array of objects with:
  {
    "canonical_url": "https://...",
    "domain": "example.com",
    "count": 2,
    "variations": ["https://...", "http://..."]  # optional with --variations
  }

## USAGE

### Basic Examples

  # Extract from text file
  ./2links input.txt

  # Extract from any format (HTML, JSON, code, etc.)
  ./2links document.html
  ./2links config.json
  ./2links source.py

  # Extract from stdin (pipe any text)
  cat page.html | ./2links
  grep -r "http" . | ./2links

  # With statistics
  ./2links input.txt --verbose

  # JSON output with variations
  ./2links urls.txt --format json --variations

  # Filter and exclude internal
  ./2links urls.txt --filter github.com --no-internal

  # Save results to file
  ./2links mixed.txt --output results.txt --no-internal

### Command-Line Options

  -f, --format FORMAT         Output format: text|json (default: text)
  -F, --filter DOMAIN         Filter URLs by domain (supports partial match)
  -o, --output FILE           Write output to file instead of stdout
  -v, --verbose               Show statistics, warnings, and counts
  -V, --variations            Include URL variations in JSON output
      --no-internal           Exclude localhost and private IP addresses
  -h, --help                  Show help message
      --version               Show version

## EDGE CASES & WARNINGS

### Detected Issues (with --verbose)

- **Internal IPs:** localhost, 127.x, 192.168.x, 10.x, 172.16-31.x
- **User Info in URLs:** user:pass@host (stripped, warned)
- **Invalid URLs:** Logged but skipped (doesn't halt processing)
- **Malformed Input:** Continues gracefully, reports counts

### Statistics Reported

- URLs found (regex matches)
- URLs valid (parse successful)
- URLs invalid (parse failed)
- Unique canonical URLs
- Total variations (all original forms)
- Internal IP detections
- User info detections

## DESIGN DECISIONS

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| Scheme-agnostic dedup key | Allows http/https equivalence without false positives |
| HTTPS preference | Security-aware default, aligns with modern practices |
| Query params in identity | Omitted (canonical URLs are stable targets, params are ephemeral) |
| No network I/O | Offline operation: fast, secure, no external dependencies |
| Stateful class design | Maintains state for chaining, multi-call workflows |
| Optional HTML parsing | Flexibility without breaking plain-text use case |

## EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Basic Text Extraction

  Input:
    Check https://github.com/user/repo
    Old link: http://github.com/user/repo

  Command:
    $ ./2links input.txt

  Output:
    https://github.com/user/repo

### Example 2: Format-Agnostic Processing

  Input (mixed formats):
    HTML: <a href="https://example.com">Example</a>
    JSON: {"url": "https://example.com"}
    Markdown: [Link](https://example.com)
    Code: URL = "https://example.com"

  Command:
    $ ./2links mixed_content.txt --format json --variations

  Output:
    [
      {
        "canonical_url": "https://example.com",
        "domain": "example.com",
        "count": 4,
        "variations": ["https://example.com"]
      }
    ]

### Example 3: Filtering and Excluding Internal

  Command:
    $ ./2links urls.txt --filter github --verbose --no-internal

  Output:
    https://github.com/user/repo1
    https://github.com/user/repo2

    [2links] Statistics:
      URLs found: 47
      URLs valid: 45
      URLs invalid: 2
      Unique canonical URLs: 23
      Total variations: 45
      Internal IPs detected: 3

